From: Juansolo457 <5344231+Juansolo457@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:29:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Enable the Quake 4 SDK's Xenon aim assist on PC behind
 pm_AimAssist

The Q4 SDK game code still carries the Xbox 360 aim assist under _XENON/_XBOX:
enemy selection in a narrow frustum around the crosshair (idPlayer::UpdateFocus)
and stick friction through usercmdGen->SetSlowJoystick(). Compile it for every
platform and gate it at runtime with pm_AimAssist (default 2, as on 360).

- SysCvar: pm_AimAssist* defined and declared unconditionally; new pm_joystickSlow
  bridges the friction percent to the engine the same way pm_isZoomed does.
- rvWeapon: restore the base AllowAutoAim()/GetAutoAimFOV() the SDK omits;
  autoAimFOV weapon key, defaulting to pm_AimAssistFOV.
- idUsercmdGenLocal: scale controller look by pm_joystickSlow (mouse untouched),
  reset it on map load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
